+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"observation","id":"obs_01M2G2AGHZT55J4AESPB6B0FPH","companyId":"example-co","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S6"],"title":"HTTP transport has no default authentication requirement; the config-override channel is itself well-guarded","description":"Gap: mcpHttpServer.ts's setupMiddlewares() (lines 306-319) is the only request gate on the HTTP transport and iterates Object.entries(this.userConfig.httpHeaders); httpHeaders defaults to {} (userConfig.ts:136-143), so by default the loop performs zero comparisons and every tool call is reachable unauthenticated. deploy/azure/bicep/params_template.json ships authMode: NOAUTH; the Azure-AD-backed authMode is only offered as a second, opt-in params file. Positive: configOverrides.ts's applyConfigOverrides() (lines 40-74) refuses to let a request header or query parameter relax readOnly (oneWayOverride(true)) or read a field marked isSecret via query parameters, so the request-override channel cannot itself be used to escalate privilege or exfiltrate configured secrets.","methods":["probe-schemas"],"subjects":[{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"}],"collectedAt":"2026-09-14T13:14:50Z","expiresAt":"2027-09-14T13:14:50Z","result":"partial","toolOutput":{"format":"sarif","path":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/314aa113-98aa-471e-941d-e1aa88798b5a/probe-schemas.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","sha256":"083528627e5887bdeea0827ad8655e5a65240c94c36785ff58a893c3b00b3170"},"evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/transports/mcpHttpServer.ts","description":"no-op header check when httpHeaders is empty, lines 306-319"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/deploy/azure/bicep/params_template.json","description":"authMode: NOAUTH default"},{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/314aa113-98aa-471e-941d-e1aa88798b5a/probe-schemas.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sa