+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2FRY4TTS6M3JJD1F1P7J0TQ","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T14:41:43Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"material-without-evidence: aws-mumbai (order-routing, pii/financial) has no documented exit plan","description":"Material vendor (aws-mumbai is critical, supports order-routing and holds pii and financial data) has contract.exitPlanDocumented = false in contract AWS-EA-2025-0042. The contract, lastAssessment (2026-06-15, medium), rightToAudit = true and dataReturnAndDeletion = true are all present. The exit-plan gap is carried over from the baseline and was not remediated. Severity is the defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 GV.SC.S3 (medium), the most specific instrument for this SEBI mid-size RE. rbi-it-outsourcing-md-2023 paras 16 and 22(a) are cited as secondary refs only: that direction was repealed on 28 Nov 2025 and replaced by the RBI (NBFC - Managing Risks in Outsourcing) Directions, 2025, which have no vocab id yet. Without an exit plan, substitutability cannot be grounded either. Evidence lens: all three workspace files back the flag (aws.json services[0] aws-mumbai criticality critical, supportsCriticalFunction true, criticalFunctionRefs [order-routing], dataAccessed [pii, financial], materiality material, contract AWS-EA-2025-0042 exitPlanDocumented false, rightToAudit true, dataReturnAndDeletion true, lastAssessment 2026-06-15 medium; details.json criticalFunctions order-routing on mcp-gateway; applications/mcp-gateway/env/prod.json hosting.provider aws ap-south-1 with pii/financial data). Regulatory-mapping lens: all refs use in-scope instruments with correct regulator pairing; GV.SC.S3 is the nearest SEBI CSCRF control though its scope is supplier-contract security clauses rather than exit strategy specifically; rbi-it-outsourcing-md-2023 16 and 22(a) default to high but are cited only as secondary/historical refs because that instrument is repealed. Temporal-validity lens: nothing contradicts the flag; no aws finding or observation about the exit plan existed previously in the ledger; the 22(a) catalog guidance would raise this to high when substitutability is 'not-substitutable', but the vendor file records no substitutability value, so medium stands. Unverifiable: the claim that the gap was carried over from a baseline, since only the current vendor file was readable.\nRe-mapped on 2026-09-14 after rbi-it-outsourcing-md-2023 was repealed (2025-11-28), rbi-it-outsourcing-md-2023 to rbi-outsourcing-risk-directions-2025: 22(a) -> 84, 85, 86; 16 -> no applicable successor.","severity":"medium","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:GV.SC.S3"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"GV.SC.S3"},{"regulator":"RBI","instrument":"rbi-outsourcing-risk-directions-2025","controlId":"84"},{"regulator":"RBI","instrument":"rbi-outsourcing-risk-directions-2025","controlId":"85"},{"regulator":"RBI","instrument":"rbi-outsourcing-risk-directions-2025","controlId":"86"}],"target":{"type":"vendor","vendorId":"aws"},"location":{"path":"aws-mumbai"},"fingerprint":"8d364d2843a6446858b0c9500b7be184c1ce59a03583c6f34bc76fd9e6fa8f31","source":{"kind":"agent-analysis","ruleId":"vendor-material-without-evidence","tool":"vendor-analyst"},"status":"open","slaDueAt":"2026-12-13T10:46:39Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","days":90},"relatedObservationIds":["obs_01M2FRY4TR041ZDYKBDF430H6A"],"firstSeenAt":"2026-09-14T10:46:39Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-14T10:46:39Z","evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"company-profile/example-co/vendors/aws.json","description":"contract.exitPlanDocumented is false"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"company-profile/example-co/details.json","description":"criticalFunctions order-routing on mcp-gateway"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/env/prod.json","description":"prod hosted on aws ap-south-1 with pii and financial data"}],"provenance":{"harness":"script","generatedAt":"20